From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:06:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Order finalized Dogecoin mining transactions after their
 parents

Optional Avalanche finalization stores the selected transaction set in canonical TxId radix order. That order can place children before parents and creates invalid Dogecoin templates when CTOR is disabled. Topologically reorder the same selected entries with lowest-ready-TxId tie breaking before serializing the block; preserve canonical order when CTOR is active. Selection, fees, resource accounting and finalization membership are unchanged.

The sequential UTXO consensus regression exposed this inherited ABC assumption in the existing enabled-preconsensus miner validity fixture. The implementation uses indexed parent edges and a ready heap, processing repeated parent references consistently without recursive traversal.

